Chapter: Empty List Branch
  cites Codex chapter General
  cites Codex chapter Lists

 Probe for BACKLOG Compiler Correctness #6.

 When an empty list literal appears in a branch of an if/then/else whose
 expected-type context is ErrorTy (let RHS, apply arg), the self-host C#
 emitter outputs new List<object>() which fails dotnet build.

Section: Definitions

  pick-direct : Boolean -> List Integer
  pick-direct (b) = if b then [1, 2, 3] else []

  pick-via-let : Boolean -> List Integer
  pick-via-let (b) =
   let xs = if b then [1, 2, 3] else []
   in xs

  pick-via-let-swapped : Boolean -> List Integer
  pick-via-let-swapped (b) =
   let xs = if b then [] else [1, 2, 3]
   in xs

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line ("direct-false  len = " ++ show (list-length (pick-direct False)))
    print-line ("let-false     len = " ++ show (list-length (pick-via-let False)))
    print-line ("let-swap-true len = " ++ show (list-length (pick-via-let-swapped True)))
  end

